# [Dawnline Scenes](dawnline_scenes)

Every conversation, reading and decision on Mereth. A scene opens for whoever walked up to
the thing or person it belongs to (and anyone standing with them); the rest of the party
carries on with their own.

Conventions, so the file stays legible:

* `if science` gates a choice to a JOB. `if skill comms >= 3` gates it to someone GOOD at
  it. `if holding coil` asks the chooser's own pack, `if party coil` everyone's.
* `check <skill> <dc> else <scene>` rolls for whoever chose it. A choice's other outcomes
  happen WHETHER OR NOT the roll works - so the payoff of a check lives on the next beat's
  continue choice, never beside the check.
* `lp <kind> <item>` records what the party has done; `if lp <kind> >= n` asks.
* An empty target `()` ends the conversation.

## [Scenes](scenes)

### [The Survey Drone](drone)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% The drone came down hard. Its camera eye still tracks you, a little late.
% Colony markings, a snapped antenna, and a data port that is still warm.

- [Pull its survey data](drone_data) if science
- [Try the data port](drone_data) ; check science 7 else drone_dead
- [Leave it]()

### [Survey Data](drone_data)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% Three days of flight logs. The last run went down a crack in the canyon wall west of the colony - "Cinder Caves, survey team in" - and the one before it circled a structure on the far ridge the log only calls THE LANTERN.

- [Mark both on the map](drone) ; discover caves, discover lantern, lp flag drone_read

### [Dead Circuits](drone_dead)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% The port sparks and the camera eye goes dark. Whatever it knew, it is keeping.

- [Leave it]()

### [The Overlook](overlook)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% East, the horizon is not dark. It is the color of a stove ring, and it is closer than it was when you landed.
% North across the canyon, on the far ridge, something tall and geometric stands against it - too regular for rock. It has a shadow the sun has not reached yet.

- [Take a long look at the structure](overlook_lantern) if science
- [Step back from the edge]()

### [The Far Ridge](overlook_lantern)
---
Speaker: lantern_voice
---
% Built, not grown. Its faces are angled like a flower that has not opened, and every one of them points at the sunrise.

- [Step back from the edge]() ; lp flag saw_lantern

### [The Patience](patience)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% A heavy-lift hauler, cowling open. There are three sockets in her engine where parts should be: an injector, a coil, and a drum of main cable.

- [Fit the injector](patience) if holding injector ; take injector, lp part injector
- [Fit the coil](patience) if holding coil ; take coil, lp part coil
- [Fit the main cable](patience) if holding cable ; take cable, lp part cable
- [Bring her engine up](patience_fitted) if lp part >= 3 ; check engineering 9 else patience_botched
- [Take the pilot's seat](patience_ready) if lp flag hauler_fixed
- [Step away]()

### [She Turns Over](patience_fitted)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% The injector coughs, catches, and holds. Every light on the flight deck comes up green at once and somebody in the square starts crying.

- [Seal the cowling](patience) ; lp flag hauler_fixed, signal lp_hauler_fixed

### [Not Yet](patience_botched)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% The coil arcs and the engine dies with a bang that brings the whole square running. Nothing is broken that was not already. Try again.

- [Step away]()

### [The Pilot's Seat](patience_ready)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% Two hundred and twelve people are already strapped in behind you. The canyon mouth is narrow, the salt beyond it is flat and featureless, and the light is coming.

- [Fly out along the surveyed road](patience_launched) if lp flag road_clear
- [Fly her out blind](patience_launched) if helm ; check helm 9 else patience_scare
- [Try to fly her out](patience_launched) ; check helm 12 else patience_scare
- [Not yet]()

### [Lift-off](patience_launched)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% She climbs. The canyon walls fall away, the salt flats blur under her, and then there is nothing below but cloud.

- [Take her up](patience) ; signal lp_launch

### [Too Close](patience_scare)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% You lose the horizon over the salt and pull up with the wingtip a meter off the ground. She is back on the pad, nobody is hurt, and nobody is speaking.

- [Try again when you are ready]()

### [The Depot Ledger](depot_ledger)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% Stock records. The injector, the coil and two other hauler parts were signed out four days ago - all on the deputy's own code, all marked "returned to supplier". Stillwater has no supplier within six light-years.

- [Copy the record](depot_ledger) if security ; lp evidence ledger
- [Note it down](depot_ledger) ; lp evidence ledger
- [Step away]()

### [The Clinic](clinic)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% A dispensary, a lab bench, and a centrifuge that still works.

- [Brew antivenom from the sample](clinic_brewed) if holding venom ; take venom, check medical 8 else clinic_spoiled
- [Step away]()

### [Antivenom](clinic_brewed)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% Two doses, faintly blue. They will not keep long in this cold.

- [Pack them](clinic) ; give antidote

### [Spoiled](clinic_spoiled)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% It separates in the centrifuge. The sample is gone. You will need another.

- [Step away]()

### [The Deputy's Terminal](office_log)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% Comms logs. Three nights ago the deputy called the Skaraan ship on a private band, and the night after he called it again, shouting. The last entry is a single line: "You get the part when I get my family on your ship."

- [Save the log](office_log) ; lp evidence log
- [Step away]()

### [Magistrate Oyelaran](oyelaran)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% A tall woman in a coat three sizes too big, with a clipboard she has clearly been holding for days. "You are the ship. Good. Sit down or stand up, but listen."

- [We are here to get you out](oyelaran_plan) ; signal lp_met_magistrate
- [What happened to the hauler?](oyelaran_hauler)
- [Tell me about the Lantern](oyelaran_lantern)
- [Where is your survey team?](oyelaran_survey)
- [Later]()

### [The Plan](oyelaran_plan)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% "Three ways, as far as I can see. Fix the Patience and fly everyone out. Or the Skaraan - their ship could take us all, and their captain knows it. Or the old stories are true and that thing on the ridge was built to keep this valley in shadow." She looks at the sky. "Pick one fast."

- [Where are the hauler's parts?](oyelaran_hauler)
- [Tell me about the Lantern](oyelaran_lantern)
- [We will be back]()

### [The Hauler](oyelaran_hauler)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% "The injector and the coil went missing four days ago. The cable is in the depot, and my deputy has the depot key, and my deputy has not been himself." She does not say anything else about that, which says a great deal.

- [Where is the deputy?](oyelaran_deputy)
- [Back]()

### [The Deputy](oyelaran_deputy)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% "Colm Harrow. His office is by the east wall. He has a wife and two children on the list for the Patience, same as everyone." A pause. "He keeps checking the Skaraan band."

- [Back]()

### [The Lantern](oyelaran_lantern)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% "The first settlers found it already here. It never did anything. The Skaraan came to dig it out a week ago, and since then the tremors have been worse and the - things - in the caves have been coming up." She shrugs. "Stories say it used to turn."

- [Back]() ; discover lantern

### [The Survey Team](oyelaran_survey)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% "Castellan and Brandt went into the Cinder Caves to see what was bringing the glassbacks up. That was three days ago. The cave mouth is at the west end of the canyon."

- [We will look for them]() ; discover caves

### [The Colonists](crowd)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% Two hundred people in coats, sitting on their luggage in the square. Children asleep across their parents' knees.
% Somebody has chalked a clock face on the ground. The hands are drawn in at sunrise.

- [Ask what they have heard](crowd_rumor)
- [Tell them to be ready to move]() ; lp flag crowd_warned

### [Talk in the Square](crowd_rumor)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% "The Skaraan paid Harrow in something - I saw him with a crate." "The glassbacks follow heat. Do not run hot in the caves." "My grandmother said the Lantern turns if you ask it right. She never said what right was."

- [Thank them]()

### [Deputy Harrow](harrow)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% A thin man who cannot keep his hands still. "If the magistrate sent you about the depot, the key is - it is around. I will find it."

- [Ask for the depot key](harrow_key) ; check comms 9 else harrow_stonewall
- [Lay out what you found](harrow_confront) if lp evidence >= 2
- [Leave him be]()

### [The Key](harrow_key)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% He hands it over like it weighs a great deal more than it does.

- [Take it]() ; give depot_key

### [Stonewalled](harrow_stonewall)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% "I said I would find it." He turns back to his terminal and does not turn round again.

- [Leave him be]()

### [The Truth](harrow_confront)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% He reads the ledger and the log you put in front of him, and sits down on the floor. "I sold them the parts so they would take my family. Then their captain said the deal was off - that she would take everybody or nobody. So I took something of hers." He points at the cellar door. "She is only a child. She is fine. I did not know what else to do."

- [Take his keys](harrow_confessed) if security
- [Take his keys](harrow_confessed) ; check security 8 else harrow_bolts

### [Keys](harrow_confessed)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% The depot key and a heavy iron one for the cellar bolt.

- [Take them]() ; give depot_key, give harrow_key, signal lp_harrow_confessed

### [He Runs](harrow_bolts)
---
Speaker: stillwater
---
% He is past you and out of the door before anyone moves. He will not get far in a canyon - but he took his keys with him.

- [Let him go]() ; signal lp_harrow_fled

