### [The Obelisk](glyph_1)
---
Speaker: lantern_voice
---
% Every face of the pillar is carved, and the carvings are not decoration: they repeat, with small changes, like a sentence being conjugated.

- [Read the carving](glyph_1_read) if science ; check science 6 else glyph_1_garbled
- [Puzzle at it](glyph_1_read) ; check science 9 else glyph_1_garbled
- [Step back]()

### [The First Panel](glyph_1_read)
---
Speaker: lantern_voice
---
% A sun, drawn as a disc with a bite out of it. Then the Lantern, open. Then the valley, dark. The verb between them is TURN, and it has a tense: WHEN ASKED.

- [Commit it to memory]() ; lp glyph 1

### [Garbled](glyph_1_garbled)
---
Speaker: lantern_voice
---
% The shapes slide around when you try to hold them. Maybe someone else would see it.

- [Step back]()

### [The Carved Wall](glyph_2)
---
Speaker: lantern_voice
---
% Smooth as glass, cold as the rest of the cave is warm. The carving here is deeper and older.

- [Read the carving](glyph_2_read) if science ; check science 7 else glyph_2_garbled
- [Puzzle at it](glyph_2_read) ; check science 10 else glyph_2_garbled
- [Step back]()

### [The Second Panel](glyph_2_read)
---
Speaker: lantern_voice
---
% The caves, drawn as veins. Heat running up them toward the Lantern. A warning mark: the Lantern DRINKS the deep heat to turn. Asked wrongly, it drinks too much.

- [Commit it to memory]() ; lp glyph 2

### [Garbled](glyph_2_garbled)
---
Speaker: lantern_voice
---
% Veins, heat, a mark you do not recognize. It slips away.

- [Step back]()

